          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "To automate order processing and shop-floor data capture without replacing your existing ERP (e.g., Pronto, Epicor, SyteLine, SAP B1, or older on-premises systems), you need a partner specializing in **ERP extension, integration architecture, and industrial low-code development**—rather than a vendor trying to sell a costly ERP rip-and-replace.\n\nIn the Australian market—and specifically accessible to Canberra/ACT—consider evaluating the following consultancies:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Consultancies with Dedicated Power Platform & Manufacturing/Integration Expertise\n\n#### **Walkerscott**\n* **Why them:** Walkerscott has a dedicated office and team in **Canberra**. They specialize in Microsoft Dynamics and the Power Platform, bridging the gap between legacy operational platforms and modern workflow automation. \n* **Fit for your project:** Ideal if you want a team with a local Canberra footprint that understands how to build custom Power Apps and automated flows on top of existing business databases without forcing a full system migration.\n\n#### **Professional Advantage**\n* **Why them:** One of Australia’s largest and most established Microsoft Solutions Partners with deep domain focus in **manufacturing, supply chain, and distribution**. \n* **Fit for your project:** Because they have both a manufacturing ERP practice and an advanced Power Platform practice, their engineers understand how to integrate into work-in-progress (WIP) tracking, bill of materials (BOM), and inventory tables without breaking ERP integrity.\n\n#### **Barhead Solutions**\n* **Why them:** Nationally recognized as one of Microsoft’s top tier-1 partners dedicated specifically to Power Platform, low-code architecture, and Business Applications. \n* **Fit for your project:** Barhead is ideal for building sophisticated **Power Automate workflows and AI Builder integrations** (e.g., automated PDF purchase-order extraction straight into your ERP) and mobile-responsive canvas apps for plant operators.\n\n#### **Antares Solutions**\n* **Why them:** Antares focuses heavily on enterprise data, systems integration, and Power Platform architecture. \n* **Fit for your project:** If your legacy ERP lacks modern open APIs, Antares specializes in building the glue layer—using Azure Integration Services, On-Premises Data Gateways, or Power Automate Desktop (RPA) to push and pull data directly to legacy databases securely.\n\n#### **Inturing / Boutique Industrial Low-Code Specialists**\n* **Why them:** Boutique firms like Inturing specialize strictly in **Power Platform and AI for Australian manufacturing and supply chain environments**. \n* **Fit for your project:** Smaller, focused firms are often faster and more agile for scoped shop-floor proofs-of-concept (e.g., deploying 3–4 tablet stations on the floor for scrap tracking, machine down-time, or batch completion in a matter of weeks).\n\n---\n\n### 2. How the Technical Architecture Should Look\nWhen speaking to these consultants, ensure they propose a solution structured around this model:\n\n1. **Intelligent Order Processing:**\n   * Incoming PDF/email customer purchase orders are routed through **Power Automate + AI Builder** (or Azure Document Intelligence) to extract line items, quantities, and delivery dates.\n   * An approval workflow (Teams or Power Apps) allows a customer service rep to review exceptions before creating a Sales Order in your ERP via an API or database connector.\n2. **Shop-Floor Data Capture:**\n   * **Power Apps (Canvas App)** deployed on ruggedised Android/iOS tablets mounted to workstations or handheld barcode/RFID scanners.\n   * Operators scan job travellers, clock labor, record machine output, flag defects, and log non-conformance without dealing with paper sheets.\n3. **The ERP Bridge:**\n   * If your ERP has REST/SOAP APIs: A **Custom Connector** is built in Power Platform.\n   * If on-premises with SQL: Microsoft’s **On-Premises Data Gateway** allows Power Platform to read/write staging tables directly and safely.\n   * If completely closed/legacy: **Power Automate Desktop (RPA)** emulates keystrokes to input completed jobs into the ERP client without user intervention.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Questions to Ask Prospective Partners\n\n1. **ERP Experience:** *\"Have you built integration pipelines into [Your ERP Name] before, and do you recommend a staging database or direct API/webhooks?\"*\n2. **Shop-Floor Usability:** *\"Can you show examples of touch/glove-friendly Power Apps that integrate with hardware barcode scanners (Zebra, Honeywell, etc.) and handle offline caching if Wi-Fi drops on the shop floor?\"*\n3. **Licensing Optimization:** *\"How will you architect shop-floor data capture to avoid paying $20+/user/month Power Apps licenses for every shift worker?\"* \n   *(A skilled partner will suggest pooled kiosk devices, Power Pages, or Azure-backed hybrid architectures to keep operational licensing low).*\n4. **Local Support:** *\"Will design, configuration, and testing be delivered locally in Australia, and who provides break-fix support if an automated ERP sync fails during production hours?\"*",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
          "role": "model"
        },
